With these changes:

1. We allocate a `sourceStats` array in `configure_` to hold `[min, max]` from each TIFF’s GDAL metadata.
2. We extract `STATISTICS_MINIMUM`/`STATISTICS_MAXIMUM` once per source (from the first image) and store them in `sourceStats`.
3. We assign `this.sourceStats_` after configuration.
4. In `loadTile_`, we pull `this.sourceStats_` into the closure and, when `source.min`/`source.max` are not user-provided, prefer the GDAL statistics before falling back to per-type defaults.
5. Thus normalization uses real image statistics if available.
